# TDD

A **discriminating assertion** fails on unfixed code and passes once the bug is fixed. Assert the user-visible result, scoped so a nearby control with the same label cannot satisfy it. When fixed and unfixed code fail the same way, debug the harness.

Recording clock, chunks, and waveform duration: `.cursor/rules/recording-ct-takeaways.mdc`.
Compare-step player refs: `.cursor/rules/compare-player-takeaways.mdc`.

## Prove red

1. Write the failing test. Run it. Expect red.
2. Apply the production fix. Run the same test. Expect green.
3. Prove red on baseline production, then restore the fix.
   - Uncommitted fix: copy each production file aside (for example `%TEMP%`), run `git checkout HEAD -- <those files>`, re-run the test, then copy the fix back.
   - Committed fix: run `git checkout HEAD~1 -- <production files>`, re-run the test, then `git checkout HEAD -- <production files>`.
   - Leave the stash stack alone. It is shared across worktrees.

When the user asks for commits, commit the test and the production fix separately.

Run Cypress from `web` as in `.cursor/rules/cypress-testing-takeaways.mdc`. Jest specs follow `.cursor/rules/jest-testing-takeaways.mdc`.
